==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|вѣ́ра||ru-PRO}}

===Etymology===
{{root|ru|ine-pro|*weh₁-}} {{dercat|ru|ine-bsl-pro|ine-pro|inh=1}}
{{inh+|ru|orv|вѣра}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*věra}}.

{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|cu|вѣра}}, {{cog|uk|ві́ра}}, {{cog|bg|вя́ра}}, {{cog/sl-tonal|vẹ́ra}}, {{cog|pl|wiara}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of {{cog|la|vērus}} and {{cog|de|wahr}}.
{{col-bottom}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|ве́ра}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-вера.ogg}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Tatiana Kerbush-вера.wav|a=Saint Petersburg}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|ве́ра}}

# [[belief]], [[faith]]
#: {{uxi|ru|'''ве́ра''' [[в]] [[кто-либо|кого́-либо]]/[[что́-либо]]|'''belief''' in someone/something}}
# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} [[trust]], [[faith]] {{gloss|belief in someone's honesty and reliability}}
# {{lb|ru|religion}} [[faith]], [[creed]] {{gloss|adherence to a religion; a set of religious beliefs}}
#: {{uxi|ru|христиа́нская '''ве́ра'''|Christian '''faith'''}}

